From: Matt Hargett <plaztiksyke@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 22:48:23 -0700
Subject: tests/disas + tests/all: pulley fusion corner-case coverage
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds 9 disas filetests + 7 integration tests covering correctness
edges in the Pulley call_indirect band+brif (phase 1) and brif+xload+
xload (phase 2) fusion stack. The shapes are drawn from known bug
classes in other engines (V8, JSC, WAMR, wasm3, WasmEdge, Hermes,
ChakraCore, Luau) where the analogous fusion shape has had soundness
or invariant-edge bugs. Each test docstring cites the upstream
precedent.

Disas filetests (`tests/disas/pulley-fusion-*.wat`):

  Gating — phase 1 / phase 2 must NOT fire:
    no-fire-user-mask                 i32 `(i32.const -2) (i32.and) (br_if)` user wasm
    no-fire-mutable-table             table.set anywhere → predicate off
    no-fire-table-fill                table.fill → predicate off
    no-fire-table-copy                table.copy → only the dst table is mutated
    no-fire-table-grow                table.grow → predicate off
    no-fire-sig-runtime-check         sig elision fails (mixed sigs in elem) → phase 2
                                      can't match, phase 1 still fires as fallback

  Firing — phase 2 MUST fire:
    fires-32bit                       pulley32 (= arm64_32-apple-watchos) target
    fires-multi-call                  two call_indirect sites in one function;
                                      each fuses independently
    fires-return-call-indirect        tail call still has the brif lazy-init
                                      check; phase 2 fires upstream of the
                                      call_indirect-vs-return_call_indirect choice

Integration tests (`tests/all/pulley.rs`, `fusion_*` family):

    fusion_call_indirect_every_index        every in-bounds index returns the right
                                            callee; OOB traps cleanly
    fusion_call_indirect_multi_site         two call_indirect sites' results compose
    fusion_return_call_indirect             tail call returns the right value
    fusion_call_indirect_with_host_null_set host Table::set null mid-execution;
                                            fused op's runtime null check fires
    fusion_call_indirect_with_host_swap     host Table::set swap to a different
                                            funcref; fused op re-loads code+vmctx
                                            on next dispatch (no stale cache)
    fusion_call_indirect_imported_table     module B imports module A's table and
                                            calls through it; correct VMFuncRef
                                            layout used across module boundary
    fusion_call_indirect_null_slot          ref.null func slot → trap, not SIGSEGV

The integration tests run a `pulley_and_native_agree` helper that
executes the same module on Pulley AND on wasmtime's native Cranelift
backend, asserting both produce the same result. Trap-expecting tests
run on Pulley only — native trap-via-signal interacts with cargo
test's debug-mode signal handlers and shows up as SIGSEGV rather than
a wasmtime Trap (the same code outside the test harness traps
cleanly). Pulley uses explicit trapz emissions (no signals) so it
works in both modes.

Upstream precedents cited in test docstrings:
    V8 issue 5913 (sig-mismatch with table-sharing)
    V8 CVE-2024-2887 / 4761 (JS-to-wasm boundary funcref injection)
    V8 CVE-2024-7971 (Liftoff non-null elision regression)
    V8 CVE-2023-4068 (WASM-null vs JS-null confusion)
    Wasmtime Winch GHSA-q49f-xg75-m9xw (table.fill host panic)
    WAMR CVE-2025-64713 (fast-interp fused-op stack overflow)
    WAMR #4041 (AOT call_indirect index > 0 broken)
    WAMR #3992 / #3993 / #4497 (call_indirect type validation)
    WAMR #2231 (return_call_indirect not tail)
    wasm3 #547 (call_indirect SEGV — missing bounds check)
    wasm3 #335 (null table element trap)
    wasm3 #513-#521 (call_indirect validation gaps)
    WasmEdge #4757 (GC null ref SEGV — null check after deref)
    WasmEdge #4292 / #4259 / #4258 (interp vs JIT divergence)
    Hermes 24a8fe64 (GC mid-IC fast-path)
    Hermes #1590 / #1801 (shape-elision corner cases)
    Hermes 5943fa4a (read/write IC cross-pollution)
    ChakraCore #5915 / #6325 (IC poisoning, type confusion)
    ChakraCore ARM IC offset PR #3436
    Luau release/717 (userdata/buffer cache invalidation)
    Luau #2358 / #234 / #2248 (GC + fused-op interaction)

Differential fuzzing (Pulley vs wasmtime native via `cargo fuzz run
differential`) was attempted but blocked locally on (a) OCaml not
installed for the wasm-spec-interpreter dep, and (b) a path-resolution
bug in `crates/fuzzing/build.rs` (`env::current_dir()` is the
cargo-fuzz build cwd, not the package dir, so the wast-test scan
fails). Both are wasm-benchmark-environment issues, not fusion bugs;
deferring as a follow-up rather than blocking on installing OCaml
or upstreaming a build.rs fix.
